mention about vulnerabilities

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.739
that have come out last week
around our modern computers,

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:06.360
and specifically
these vulnerabilities

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.580
are related to
modern processors.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.130
And they impact things like
your personal computer,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.070
your mobile devices,
and the cloud.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.130
Now, there is a lot
of content out there.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.000
There's many different links,
and we'll definitely provide

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.650
some of these on our website.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.630
And we have some
great information

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.690
that our security group
has done on this on a blog

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.800
that we will provide
around GCP and how they're

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.192
working to support that.

00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:31.650
But the main thing
to understand is

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.630
that Meltdown and Spectre
are two vulnerabilities

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.830
that you want to be aware of.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.690
You want to make sure you're
updating your operating system.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.580
You want to make sure
that you are updating

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.580
all the things whenever
you have the opportunity

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.230
to on your phones, on your
laptops, on whatever cloud

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.665
services you're working with.

00:01:44.665 --> 00:01:47.290
And Mark-- I think you wanted to
touch on this briefly as well?

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:47.730
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.560
